findings.body:
The setter check changed from `value <= 0` to `value < 0`, so `RetainedFileCountLimit = 0` is accepted. The XML doc in this same PR says the value is "a strictly positive value", and the exception message still says "must be positive". The provider only prunes when `_maxRetainedFiles > 0`, so 0 quietly means retain every file forever.

::diff{file="src/Logging.AzureAppServices/src/AzureFileLoggerOptions.cs" lines="48-58"}

::callout{type="warning"}
A user who sets 0 expecting "keep no files" gets unbounded growth with no error. The old `<= 0` check caught this, so this change is a regression, not a doc fix.

If the intent is to allow 0, the docs and message have to say what 0 means. If not, the old check should be restored.

The setter changed from `value < 0` to `value <= 0`, so `BackgroundQueueSize = 0` now throws. This is a behavior change, and it is not mentioned in the PR description or the XML docs. The message still says "must be non-negative", which now contradicts the check.

::diff{file="src/Logging.AzureAppServices/src/BatchingLoggerOptions.cs" lines="42-54"}

Rejecting 0 is probably correct: `BatchingLoggerProvider` builds a `BlockingCollection` with this bound, and a bound of 0 would throw there anyway, so this moves the failure earlier. The fix still has to ship with the message corrected to "must be positive" and a note that 0 is now invalid. Any existing caller that passes 0 will now fail at configuration time.

`TryGetValidatableTypeInfo` used to set `validatableTypeInfo = null` after the loop, which guaranteed a null out value whenever nothing matched. The PR moved that assignment to the top of the method. If a resolver returns `false` after writing a non-null value to its out parameter, that value now reaches the caller even though the method returns false.

::diff{file="src/Validation/src/ValidationOptions.cs" lines="44-58"}

The XML doc still says the out value is "otherwise, null". The sibling `TryGetValidatableParameterInfo` keeps the reset after the loop, so the two methods now behave differently. Restore the reset after the loop, which is the pattern in the sibling method.

The signature for `TryGetValidatableParameterInfo` now ends with `) {` on the same line. The rest of the file, including the sibling method, puts the opening brace on its own line.

::diff{file="src/Validation/src/ValidationOptions.cs" lines="65-67"}

This is a formatting nit, but the repository's analyzers and formatter will flag it, and it is unrelated to the documentation change.
